From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Dmitry Afonchenko <undermove1@gmail.com>
Date: Fri, 30 Oct 2026 10:57:24 +0400
Subject: [PATCH 55/77] Meridian: don't quarantine every file child processes
 write

LSFileQuarantineEnabled made files written by Workbench terminals and local
agents quarantined, so OpenCode's unpacked libopentui.dylib raised a
Gatekeeper warning on every status check. Downloads stay quarantined by the
download code.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Claude-Session: https://claude.ai/code/session_01SwxrQ2eLfJ2bv8cCoG2va1
---
 chrome/app/app-Info.plist | 6 ++++--
 1 file changed, 4 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/chrome/app/app-Info.plist b/chrome/app/app-Info.plist
index 6fada0a2b1..4f9092a2ef 100644
--- a/chrome/app/app-Info.plist
+++ b/chrome/app/app-Info.plist
@@ -207,8 +207,10 @@
 		<key>MallocNanoZone</key>
 		<string>0</string>
 	</dict>
-	<key>LSFileQuarantineEnabled</key>
-	<true/>
+	<!-- Meridian: no LSFileQuarantineEnabled. With it every file that a
+	     Workbench terminal or a local agent writes got quarantined, so tools that
+	     unpack a library at run time (OpenCode) raised Gatekeeper warnings.
+	     Downloads are still quarantined explicitly by the download code. -->
 	<key>LSHasLocalizedDisplayName</key>
 	<string>1</string>
 	<key>LSMinimumSystemVersion</key>
